Below is the change description:
The current Spring AI OpenAI implementation relies on direct REST/WebClient calls. The project is migrating towards utilizing the official OpenAI Java SDK for better maintenance, stability, and access to new features. This change provides the necessary infrastructure to use the official SDK for text-to-speech functionality, enabling users to choose between the legacy REST-based implementation and the new SDK-based one via configuration properties.
Introduced support for OpenAI Audio Speech using the official OpenAI Java SDK by adding OpenAiSdkAudioSpeechModel, OpenAiSdkAudioSpeechOptions, and their corresponding auto-configuration (OpenAiSdkAudioSpeechAutoConfiguration) and property classes. Added necessary metadata handling for rate limits via OpenAiSdkAudioSpeechResponseMetadata and created corresponding integration and unit tests.

